      "role": "user",
      "content": "hm, okay, so it's a discrepancy in how the tests are being applied. if the p-value is one-tailed and the interval is two-tailed, that would explain it. but it still feels weirdly messy. it's like there's this hidden error or something causing the data to not behave the way the math says it should. is it common in social science for there to be this kind of \"noise\" or randomness that just messes up the clean logic of the models?",
